{"title":"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2><p>\nFind the number of ordered pairs of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> which satisfy </p><center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/b/9db3357e293b63851ef1642c66d41e9e2bb2aad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+4xy+y^2=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" />.</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We look at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/9/029cdfb3634328533466c749372b7520f027b36b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/f/96f0c2605ee421c29d4e905a6538b512e15d6124.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\equiv 0\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />\n<ul><li>Case 1a: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/5/e5545ffdaa5d526655c8ea1a22d71dd70ea79183.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y\\equiv 0\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />: Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/a/56ab01cceb4cae05a7dbee18d8f1b558beb7f858.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+4xy+y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee19f2230cc721282aa8253c8d9b7e5ff8ffbe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2=9$\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> isn't.</li>\n<li>Case 1b: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/8/6985143755d9114ff71e8a68c06aa48dafe2cd01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y\\equiv 1\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />: Then the LHS is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c66dfe80a14eba051f449b79732ace3cfd6ad65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, while the RHS isn't.</li>\n<li>Case 1c: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/7/a87f701bf13f75c4a2100e14acd794c2e57b2ba4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y\\equiv 2\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" />: Then the LHS is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c66dfe80a14eba051f449b79732ace3cfd6ad65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, while the RHS isn't.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Case 2: x=1mod3\n<ul><li>Case 2a: y=0mod3: This is equivalent to case 1b.</li>\n<li>Case 2b: y=1mod3: We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/1/34179847721223308b658caa729abaad9f01d95b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=3x_1+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/6/0e6253a9c6711291d3c5864f9196f77820365f84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=3y_1+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" />:</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd60d33a25eb49441278d0ee7041ddf686f51a46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+4xy+y^2=21=(3x_1+1)^2+4(3x_1+1)(3y_1+1)+(3y_1+1)^2=9(x^2+y^2+4x_1y_1+2x_1+2y_1)+6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"827\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>But 21 isn't 6mod9, it's 3mod9.\n</p>\n<ul><li><ul><li>Case 2c: y=2mod3: Then the LHS is 1mod3 while the RHS isn't.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Case 3: x=2mod3\n<ul><li>Case 3a: y=0mod3: This is equivalent to case 1c.</li>\n<li>Case 3b: y=1mod3: This is equivalent to case 2c.</li>\n<li>Case 3c: y=2mod3: We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e0073e39e79b885510f95012c1a53741c6f05122.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=3x_1+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/f/41f3247ebdeefe6fc04d76be681517198435d829.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=3y_1+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" />:</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/4/884872ee499971e9402be91b1995b0c16bca9d03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+4xy+y^2=21=(3x_1+2)^2+4(3x_1+2)(3y_1+2)+(3y_1+2)^2=9(x_1^2+y_1^2+4x_1y_1+4x_1+4y_1+2)+6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"859\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>But 21 isn't 6mod9, it's 3mod9.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f1406b65f9f2e6a365b7356da731780b42cceb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\]\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/032fe817d76bd6ff1daf08386b7148b70d91b31f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Consider the equation: } x^2 + 4xy + y^2 = 21\\]\" width=\"321\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/b/78b25b03dccd443715c39f4c4a0c703b072d5d3d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Notice it looks similar to a perfect square: } x^2 + 2xy + y^2 = (x+y)^2\\]\" width=\"508\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/8/9a82db043fd9bc83612393468d9a4c89b8dda204.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Alternatively, we can write it as } (x+y)^2 + 2xy\\]\" width=\"352\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d109c29396103ff2ccc98b22dc9d361a09216e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Now, } 21 \\text{ cannot be written as a sum of a perfect square and twice a product of integers, i.e there is no solution }\\]\" width=\"808\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/6/e3679a77e82d6c28b0ece048fce46a2349b9487c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Hence, there are no integer solutions.}\\]\" width=\"269\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=~Trashboycan\" title=\"~Trashboycan\">~Trashboycan</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST\">2005 Alabama ARML TST</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017205231\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 1.342 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 201/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1380/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 213/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5137/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.530      1 Template:ARML_box\n100.00%    7.530      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5940:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017205231 and revision id 280650. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}